  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If the margin made on an article costing \\(C\\) dollars and selling for \\(S\\) dollars is \\(M=\\dfrac1nC,\\) then the margin is given by:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(M=\\dfrac1{n-1}S\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(M=\\dfrac1nS\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(M=\\dfrac n{n+1}S\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(M=\\dfrac1{n+1}S\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(M=\\dfrac n{n-1}S\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p23.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(S=C+M=C+\\frac{C}{n},\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} S&=\\frac{n+1}{n}C,\\\\ C&=\\frac n{n+1}S. \\end{aligned} \\] Therefore \\[ M=\\frac Cn=\\frac1{n+1}S. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(S=C+M\\) together with \\(M=\\frac{C}{n}\\)",
        "Express \\(C\\) in terms of \\(S\\), then divide by \\(n\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
